{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# Phase 2 report — FIXED (rebar-debug). Gerrit change 1435.\n\nPhase 1 RCA is in the first comment. This is what changed and the evidence.\n\n## Already captured vs newly persisted\n\nThe scope note was right: a WIRING job. `failure_usage()` (`usage_log.py:136-191`) already\nreduced a run's messages to the complete loop-vs-breadth signal; `record()` built its row from\n`_FIELDS` alone and dropped seven keys one frame from the write. No second mechanism was built —\nthe success path now calls THE SAME reducer.\n\n| field | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| four token counters + `requests` | persisted | unchanged |\n| `tool_calls`, `tool_calls_distinct`, `max_consecutive_repeat`, `top_repeated_tool_calls`, `request_limit`, `tool_calls_limit`, `finish_reason` | **computed then discarded** | persisted, BOTH paths |\n| `duration_s`, `ticket` | did not exist | persisted |\n| a gate run with no env var set | **recorded nothing at all** | records to `.rebar/usage.jsonl` |\n\n## Where it lives + retrieval\n\n`REBAR_USAGE_LOG` still wins when set. Unset, a run inside a GATE SESSION appends to\n`<repo root>/.rebar/usage.jsonl`. The predicate is the existing fail-closed `in_gate_session()`\nthat every code-reading gate binds through the one chokepoint `gate_source.gate_read_root`\n(`gate_source.py:110`; entered by `plan_review/__init__.py:459` and `completion.py:485`) — no new\nplumbing. Outside a gate session with the var unset, `record()` still writes nothing at all.\n\n    python -m rebar.llm.usage_log summarize .rebar/usage.jsonl\n\n## PROOF — a real gate run, never instrumented\n\n`REBAR_USAGE_LOG` confirmed unset (`env | grep -c` -> 0), then `rebar review-plan aec1-...`:\n\n    plan-review-prerequisite-verifier  failed  requests=0  tool_calls=0  duration=185.6s\n    ticket-digest                      ok      requests=1  tool_calls=0  duration=6.1s\n    overlap-judge                      ok      requests=1  tool_calls=0  duration=4.7s\n    overlap-judge                      ok      requests=1  tool_calls=0  duration=17.2s\n    overlap-judge                      ok      requests=1  tool_calls=0  duration=4.7s\n\nRow 1 in full: step=prerequisite_verify, model=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6,\nrequest_limit=125, tool_calls_limit=250, tool_calls_distinct=0, max_consecutive_repeat=0,\ntop_repeated_tool_calls=[], duration_s=185.6. **A FAILED call that burned three minutes and\npreviously left no trace of any kind.** `summarize` folds it, priced:\n`| **total** | **4** | **13014** | **942** | **1796** | **1796** | **3** | **$0.0412** |`\n`git status` stays clean — `.rebar/*` is already gitignored.\n\n## RED evidence + mutation check\n\n`tests/unit/test_usage_log_run_shape_aec1.py` was written FIRST and held OUT of the fix\nsubagent's working tree. RED for the right reasons (not import errors):\n`KeyError: 'tool_calls'` (exhaustion), `KeyError: 'tool_calls'` (success),\n`KeyError: 'tool_calls_distinct'`, `KeyError: 'duration_s'`,\n`AttributeError: _repo_root_for_default_sink` -> 6 failed, 1 passed.\nThen GREEN 7/7 against an oracle the fixer never saw.\n\nTwo defect-seeded mutations, each re-introducing a confirmed root cause:\n- remove the `_SHAPE_FIELDS` write in `record()` -> **4 failed**, same original KeyErrors\n- disable the gate default sink -> **1 failed** (\"a gate run recorded nothing without\n  REBAR_USAGE_LOG\")\nBoth restored to 7/7. The tests that stayed green under mutation 1 test different mechanisms,\nso the oracle discriminates rather than blanket-failing.\n\n## BOTH paths write — the axis varies\n\nThree fixtures: `_ok_model` (success), `_breadth_model` (all-distinct, terminates),\n`_looping_model` (one repeated signature, runs to budget exhaustion).\n`test_a_loop_and_a_breadth_run_are_separable_from_the_record_alone` asserts the ratio separates\nthem FROM THE DURABLE RECORD ALONE: breadth 5/5 = 1.00 vs loop 1/125 = 0.008. The four live\nmeasured examples reproduce from the same two fields (238/258 = 0.922 healthy; 76/257 = 0.296,\n167/270 = 0.619, 135/264 = 0.511 pathological).\n`test_a_non_gate_run_still_writes_nothing_when_unset` is the control in the OTHER direction —\nwithout it the gate-sink test would pass for the trivial reason that everything writes.\n\n## Coordination with 70bc — field naming\n\nI invented no vocabulary. The record uses the names `_repetition_summary()` already mints:\n`tool_calls`, `tool_calls_distinct`, `max_consecutive_repeat`, `top_repeated_tool_calls`. 70bc\nshould adopt these rather than either of us minting a second set.\n\nLIMITATION, stated rather than papered over: these are WHOLE-RUN counts. They reproduce every\nratio in the four measured examples (the stated minimum), but a WINDOWED ratio at an arbitrary\nwindow cannot be recomputed from aggregates, because the signature SEQUENCE is not stored\n(deliberately — it would grow the row without bound). If 70bc pins a window size, the natural\nextension is to emit per-window ratios at that size from the same `_repetition_summary` seam.\n\n## Siblings (Step 7, both axes)\n\nCONSTRUCT sweep (class: a fixed allowlist admitting the LIMIT and dropping the MEASUREMENT).\nSwept every allowlist constant under `src/rebar`, each hit confirmed semantically not by string\nmatch. Exactly one live sibling: `failure.py:82-96` `_ALLOWED_FIELDS` carries `request_limit` and\n`tool_calls_limit` but neither `requests` nor `tool_calls`. `_FIELDS`/`_TOKEN_FIELDS` narrowings\nare deliberate and correct; the parsing/validation allowlists are not this class.\n\nPARITY sweep (rule: a durable record of a gate call must carry what it CONSUMED, not only what it\nwas allowed to consume). usage-log JSONL = FIXED. Gate-error sidecar = MISSING (and 5 of 6\n`emit_gate_error` sites pass no diagnostic at all). Completion verdict sidecar = MISSING (no\ncounts, no duration — while plan-review's already has `requests` + a `metrics` block, so the two\ngates are asymmetric and the completion gate is the blind one). Signed attestation manifest =\nN/A WITH REASON: deliberately timestamp-free so re-signing reproduces\n(`transition_close.py:129-130`), so a run-varying metric structurally cannot live there.\n\nDISPOSITION: every MISSING slot filed as **df94-66ba-dbf8-4ac1**, linked `discovered_from` this\nticket. Not folded in here because `_ALLOWED_FIELDS` is a SANITIZATION boundary — widening it is a\nprivacy decision deserving its own review, not a ride-along on a telemetry fix.\n\n## Residual risk\n\n- **Unbounded growth.** `.rebar/usage.jsonl` is append-only and nothing prunes it. ACCEPTED and\n  documented (append-only, gitignored, never read back by rebar, safe to delete any time) — the\n  same caveat `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:200-211` already records for the review-bot sink.\n  Rotation would be new machinery on a bug fix.\n- **`ticket` is absent in practice for plan-review's own ops.** The field is wired and tested end\n  to end, but plan-review builds its `RunRequest`s with an empty `target`, so there is no\n  `ticket_id` and `record()` correctly omits the key (visible in the real rows above). ACCEPTED;\n  populating `target` at those call sites is a separate change.\n- **First-run leak-guard interaction.** If a gate runs CONCURRENTLY with the test suite, the\n  first-ever creation of `.rebar/usage.jsonl` is a new REPO_ROOT entry and the suite's leak guard\n  flags whichever test is in flight. Only on first creation; appends are not new entries. ACCEPTED,\n  recorded here so the next reader is not misled — it cost me a false conclusion (below).\n\n## A false conclusion this session, and the controls that caught it\n\nI first saw a live gate run write nothing and nearly reported the fix broken. Three controls\ncorrected it: (1) `rebar review-code` is DISABLED in this project, so that run made zero LLM calls\n— a vacuous experiment; (2) plain untracked control files placed in `.rebar/` vanished within 30s\nTOO, proving the deletion was environmental (the suite's leak guard `rmtree`), not my code; (3) the\nfirst full-suite run's 18 errors included four reading literally \"Test moved the repo HEAD\n(34998a2ca8 -> 902ee42663)\" — MY OWN COMMIT, made while the suite ran — and the rest were my manual\nprobe files. Re-running exactly those gate tests cleanly: **121 passed**.\n\n## Files changed (Gerrit 1435)\n\n    src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py   _SHAPE_FIELDS, shape_only(), run_shape alias, _resolve_sink()/\n                                 _repo_root_for_default_sink(), duration_s+ticket on record()\n                                 and record_failure()                                  [754 LOC]\n    src/rebar/llm/runner.py      success-path shape via the SAME reducer; duration+ticket [785]\n    src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py  record_call_spend forwards duration_s/ticket            [189]\n    docs/llm-framework.md        run-shape fields, default gate sink, retrieval, lifecycle\n    tests/unit/test_usage_log_run_shape_aec1.py   NEW — the held-out RED->GREEN oracle\n\nNo existing test modified, weakened, skipped or xfailed (`git diff --stat -- tests/` empty). No new\ndependency (`typing.Any` is stdlib; `rebar.config` / `rebar.llm.config` are lazy in-tree imports).\nAll modules under the 800 cap. lint = 0, typecheck = 0.\n\nOVERLAP NOTE for the agent on c827/70bc: `agent_call.py` is touched (7 lines, two optional kwargs\nforwarded). `structured_run.py`'s `failure_usage` call sites are UNTOUCHED — which is exactly why\n`failure_usage` was ALIASED (`run_shape = failure_usage`) rather than renamed. `workflow/runs.py`\nis untouched."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785951946816885001,"uuid":"4c1d2bd8-0025-4c82-a4bc-52fb836ae409"}